A1. What you must have if you want to get ahead. ~ SPEED
A5. What no-arm drivers of the gay nineties rode in. ~ PHAETON
A11. What Rockefeller's money all gathered together would make. ~ HEAP
A12. What was "life" according to Longfellow? ~ REAL
A13. This means "before." ~ ERE
A14. Only skillful people have this. ~ ART
A15. Free from pain or annoyance. ~ EASY
A16. Tail bearers of a pre-Piltdown era. ~ APES
A17. This is way up in the world (abbr.). ~ MT
A18. What it takes to get a sucker. ~ BAIT
A19. You must grind to get this. ~ GRIST
A20. The kind of stuff prosecuting attorneys are made of. ~ HARD
A21. A lady of Arthur's court—unjustly defamed. ~ ENID
A22. These are elliptical figures. ~ OVALS
A24. An exclamation—used by comic-strip Englishmen. ~ EGAD
A25. To accomplish. ~ DO
A27. What the spring does. ~ OOZE
A28. This kind of person never gets anywhere these days. ~ SLOW
A29. This spoils the best radio program. ~ SOS
A30. A city on an island with an ancient cathedral, church and monastery. ~ ELY
A31. What a clinging vine becomes. ~ BOSS
A32. These are always on foot. ~ TOES
A33. What motorists should keep to (abbr.). ~ RT
A34. A plant which furnishes a well-known drug. ~ ALOE
A35. The first Hebrew month. ~ TISRI
A36. How some people find the door to success. ~ SHUT
A37. What a certain kind of sheik lives on. ~ FARO
A38. What a Peace Conference usually ends up in. ~ MELEE
A40. This has a kick in it. ~ MULE
A41. Printer's dessert. ~ PI
A42. This has an air about it. ~ ARIA
A43. This holds a lot of liquor. ~ CASK
A44. The price you pay. ~ FEE
A45. These have the goods with them. ~ PEDDLERS
A46. Measure of length. ~ YARD

D1. Someone known for his efficient head work. ~ SHAMPOOER
D2. Indecorously free. ~ PERT
D3. What some foolish people do in night clubs. ~ EAT
D4. Eager politicians (abbr.). ~ EP
D5. This is deadly. ~ PEST
D6. What the old gray mare likes very much to hit. ~ HAY
D7. The man who should write "The Winning of the Wets." ~ AL
D8. This isn't so hot. ~ TEPID
D9. These are worth digging for. (Ask any gold-digger). ~ ORES
D10. Where the wise old bird spends the evening. ~ NEST
D12. What enforcement officers do for a drink. ~ RAID
D15. Receiving apparatuses. ~ EARS
D16. This is very dry. ~ ARID
D18. What vertical 6 comes in. ~ BALE
D19. This has a bite in it. ~ GNAW
D20. This is foggy. ~ HAZY
D21. Use these and boost yourself. ~ EGOS
D23. A unit of electro motive force. ~ VOLT
D24. Otherwise. ~ ELSE
D25. This kind of person is sure to get things done. ~ DOER
D26. What reform society heads invariably become. ~ OSSIFIED
D28. This gives you the dirt. ~ SOOT
D29. Tolerably. (Two words) ~ SOSO
D31. How you feel when you're sad. ~ BLUE
D32. This gets the air. ~ TIRE
D34. You'll never be behind as long as you are this. ~ AHEAD
D35. You'll have words if you do this. ~ TALK
D36. What the man with a skate on did. ~ SLID
D37. A senatorial debate. ~ FUSS
D38. What to see the world on. ~ MAP
D39. Before. ~ ERE
D40. What prize fighters try to do to each other. ~ MAR
D41. By the way of. ~ PER
D43. This fellow looks the land over first (init.). ~ CE
D44. A note in the musical scale. ~ FA


